{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>He turns</b> — the poet returns to proclaim the might of HaShem, as though He does a thing and its opposite according to His wisdom. He finished mentioning the sea and returned to mention the rivers that flow into it." "<b>And the meaning of \"a desert\"</b> — a land of drought." "<b>And springs of water</b> — these are the fountains."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {0 "Resolved השם as HaShem per divine-name protocol."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:02.548465807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}